MOSS-TTSD v1.0, converted for MLX (8-bit) by AudioSmith
Copyright 2026 OpenMOSS (the OpenMOSS team and MOSI.AI)

This repository redistributes, in converted form, the weights of
  - OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-TTSD-v1.0 (https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-TTSD-v1.0,
    revision c7cd852d87aff71cab5bd2b9b05509cedc0ef1ba), and
  - OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Audio-Tokenizer (https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Audio-Tokenizer,
    revision 3cd226ba2947efa357ef453bcad111b6eafba782),
both licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). The
language model is a fine-tune of Qwen3-8B (Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud),
Apache License 2.0.

Changes made by AudioSmith (https://github.com/hehehai/AudioSmith):
  - MOSS-TTSD's Linear and Embedding layers (the Qwen3 backbone, the 16
    audio embeddings and the 17 heads) quantized to 8 bits (MLX affine,
    group size 64, bfloat16 scales and biases); names and other weights
    unchanged; config.json gains a "quantization" field and loses auto_map;
  - MOSS-Audio-Tokenizer converted to codec.safetensors: weight norm folded,
    1×1 convolutions stored as matrices, attention projections renamed
    (in_projs.0 → in_proj), only the first 16 of its 32 quantizers kept (the
    ones MOSS-TTSD reads), and its Linear layers whose input size is a
    multiple of 64 quantized to 8 bits (float32 scales); codec_config.json is
    its config.json with num_quantizers 16 and a "quantization" field;
  - the tokenizer and generation files are upstream's, unchanged.
The conversion is scripts/mossttsd/convert.py in the AudioSmith repository at
the commit recorded in conversion.json.
